1
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:51,009
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,809
Sangwon Police Major Crimes Unit.
Mr. Park Hae-kang?

3
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:01,352
You're under arrest

4
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:03,062
for embezzlement and breach of trust.

5
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:06,774
Due to the risk of flight,
we're arresting you without a warrant.

6
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:09,110
You have the right to retain an attorney,

7
00:01:09,111 --> 00:01:11,196
to present your defense,
and to remain silent.

8
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:14,115
Anything you say can
and will be used against you--

9
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:14,991
Let's go.

10
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:21,248
There he is!

11
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:32,384
Just a moment.

12
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:35,636
THE TRUTH BEHIND THE TRUE VALUE STATE SCAM

13
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,430
HUMAN SCUM DESERVE MERCILESS PUNISHMENT

14
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:41,768
Let's keep moving.

15
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,105
I supported you!

16
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,149
I feel so betrayed!

17
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:58,577
Wait!

18
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,459
Guys! Don't!

19
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,670
How can you do this when you're a mom?

20
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:10,714
Mr. Park!

21
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,425
Take care of our family.

22
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:22,309
Boss!

23
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:26,646
Boss!

24
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:47,500
THE APARTMENT JOB

25
00:02:56,718 --> 00:02:59,219
You came up with great lines, Mr. Kim.

26
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,387
Good job.

27
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,181
I like the photos too.

28
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,768
It's been a while
since I got such an adrenaline rush.

29
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,312
Should I put this on my living room wall?

30
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:11,565
I can look at it whenever I'm sad.
It'll help with my depression.

31
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:13,734
We stuck about 1,000 posters
around the complex

32
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,527
and placed them in all the mailboxes.

33
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:19,574
By tomorrow,
everyone will know about Park Hae-kang.

34
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:21,867
Right.

35
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:24,370
This is the scary thing
about an apartment complex.

36
00:03:24,371 --> 00:03:28,040
Once you're branded as a fraud,
you can't step outside your door.

37
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,460
All 9,800 households will be watching him.

38
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,463
How would he endure that?

39
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,007
- Mr. Kim.
- Yes, sir.

40
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,718
Forget about eating healthy today.

41
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:42,222
How about some spicy rice cakes?
I want them very spicy.

42
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,476
So spicy

43
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:49,312
that it'll bring tears to your eyes.

44
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:01,073
I know your situation,
but give us the ledger.

45
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,158
We need to save our boss.

46
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,245
Ha-ri, give them the ledger.

47
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:07,621
It was an emergency arrest.

48
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:10,416
They have to release him
if they can't get a warrant in 48 hours.

49
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:13,669
But who knows what will happen to him
within the 48 hours?

50
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,921
There's no point in bringing the ledger.

51
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,464
Lee Chung-won's name

52
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:19,467
isn't even written in there.

53
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:25,431
<i>The names written there
were President Seo and Mr. Choi.</i>

54
00:04:25,432 --> 00:04:28,685
There's no connection
to Lee Chung-won whatsoever.

55
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:36,108
Back then, I didn't know
that Lee Chung-won was behind it.

56
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:39,028
But I've met him in person,
so if I testify...

57
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:40,237
Don't you get it?

58
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,989
Lee Chung-won planned all this.

59
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:44,575
If we bring the ledger,
it will only help him.

60
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:48,120
You mean he'll pin the blame
on Mr. Choi, President Seo,

61
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:51,166
and Ms. Kang Ha-jeong
once he gets his hands on the ledger?

62
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:57,756
I recorded everything in a way
that it'd be really easy for him

63
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:00,383
to shift all the blame to us.

64
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:03,178
Well, I...

65
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:06,014
Then...

66
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,308
what about our boss?

67
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,854
Lee Chung-won's trying to pressure us.

68
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:15,272
He wants our fake family to scatter

69
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:17,983
and disappear from this apartment complex.

70
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,651
What Lee Chung-won wanted

71
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:21,653
was the image
of Park Hae-kang getting arrested

72
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,238
so it would rattle the residents.

73
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,825
So what? We just do nothing?

74
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:28,160
He'll be released in 48 hours.

75
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,496
Forty-eight...

76
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,372
Also,

77
00:05:31,373 --> 00:05:34,750
didn't you hear Mr. Park telling us
to take care of the family?

78
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,460
We should be sticking together.

79
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:38,588
Stick together and do what?

80
00:05:39,381 --> 00:05:41,716
We have to stay right here, as a family.

81
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:46,303
If we all flee because of this,
we'll really become frauds.

82
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,597
It's true we're a fake family,

83
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:50,100
but we didn't embezzle anything.

84
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,273
So if we run away, we become frauds,

85
00:05:58,525 --> 00:06:01,111
and if we stay, we remain a family?

86
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:05,198
So we should stay here
and be a real family

87
00:06:05,949 --> 00:06:09,077
so Mr. Park can return and fight, right?

88
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:11,246
Yes.

89
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:14,791
All 9,800 households are watching us.

90
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:32,307
The system clearly says
there's 17.8 billion.

91
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:34,101
How is the account empty?

92
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:36,937
We had no idea that the account
didn't match the system.

93
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,898
We only found out today.

94
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:44,403
You practically gave away the key
to someone who made a fake family

95
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:47,072
to embezzle
the long-term repair reserve fund!

96
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:49,449
And we had no idea!

97
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:53,245
We were stupidly praising him
and calling him President Park!

98
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,329
We're sorry.

99
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:56,498
We really had no idea.

100
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:59,793
President Park managed the seal
and account himself.

101
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,795
How is that an excuse?

102
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:05,216
But we won't even be able to pay
the cleaning company next month.

103
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:08,136
To keep the complex running,

104
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:11,555
we'll have to collect a special assessment

105
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:13,682
of about 1.82 million won per household.

106
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,517
What? 1.82 million?

107
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,686
Are you kidding me?

108
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:20,689
Why should I pay for the money
that Park Hae-kang pocketed?

109
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:22,983
I'm never going to pay for that!

110
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:26,154
That 1.82 million won
isn't the problem right now!

111
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:29,490
The kindergarten's closed down
due to shoddy construction,

112
00:07:29,491 --> 00:07:32,493
the maintenance fees are out of control,
and the reserve fund is gone.

113
00:07:32,494 --> 00:07:34,369
If word spreads about this,

114
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,538
our property value will plummet!

115
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,291
Our apartment complex
could really go under overnight.

116
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:42,044
We should freeze the assets
of that scammer family

117
00:07:42,045 --> 00:07:44,923
and cut off
all their electricity and water!

118
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:50,552
Do you really think
we got scammed by them?

119
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:51,763
I can't believe it either.

120
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:54,974
The problem is his face.

121
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:57,643
How could a fraud look like that?

122
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:59,394
His acting was way too good.

123
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:01,021
Forget his face.

124
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,814
He's a fraud

125
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:04,399
who embezzled all our money.

126
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,401
Hey.

127
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,987
You have no loyalty at all.

128
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:12,241
You shouldn't treat him like this.

129
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:16,662
Did you forget who stepped up
and helped with the kindergarten issue?

130
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:18,038
That's not all.

131
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:21,125
Remember what he did about
the deliveries and the heating bills?

132
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,252
Then what about this?

133
00:08:23,253 --> 00:08:25,087
There's a photo of him at the bank.

134
00:08:25,088 --> 00:08:27,423
We're not sure what to believe anymore.

135
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:31,051
It's simple. You should trust the money.

136
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:33,470
That 17.8 billion isn't some pocket money.

137
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:36,223
If he really took all that,
why would he remain here

138
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:38,016
and work so hard?

139
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,476
Does that make any sense?

140
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:41,436
If he really embezzled 17.8 billion,

141
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,146
he would've changed his identity

142
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:46,025
and already fled the country,
don't you think?

143
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:47,485
You're right.

144
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:51,948
Before we think about whether
Park Hae-kang's a fraud or not,

145
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:55,200
we should think about finding
our 17.8 billion won.

146
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:59,205
You young mothers,
use your brains, will you?

147
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:03,751
This is tough.

148
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:05,878
My goodness.

149
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,424
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

150
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:17,389
How can this be the face of someone
who took 17.8 billion won?

151
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:21,185
He looks like
he's the one who got robbed blind.

152
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:36,159
EXPOSING PARK HAE-KANG'S CORRUPTION

153
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:37,744
<i>I swear</i>

154
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:43,374
that I have not taken so much
as a single penny in illicit gains.

155
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:46,002
I promise to cooperate

156
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,714
with any investigations.

157
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:53,551
Lastly, I sincerely apologize
to all the residents

158
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:56,095
of True Value.

159
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,565
Cut! Okay!

160
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,234
Good job.

161
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:12,695
Mr. Choi,

162
00:10:13,655 --> 00:10:15,573
you saw President Seo last time, right?

163
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:25,082
A disappearance

164
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:26,959
is neat and convenient.

165
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:30,546
No body, no evidence.

166
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,341
It only leaves hope

167
00:10:33,925 --> 00:10:36,219
for their family.

168
00:10:36,803 --> 00:10:40,223
You know that's the state
President Seo is in, don't you?

169
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,267
Yes.

170
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:47,980
I'll do anything you ask, sir.

171
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,568
I'm counting on you.

172
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,575
I need to live.

173
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,328
I have to survive first.

174
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,723
Mr. Choi.

175
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:24,725
What?

176
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,312
Where are you going?

177
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,730
I have urgent business...

178
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,441
By any chance,

179
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:33,818
are you running away?

180
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,488
Running away? No, I need to go...

181
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:38,989
Let me talk to you.

182
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,449
Is it true

183
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:42,994
that President Park
embezzled the reserve fund?

184
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:46,079
He didn't.
It was President Seo, wasn't it?

185
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,623
You and President Seo
embezzled the fund, didn't you?

186
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:49,666
Didn't you?

187
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:52,127
- Let go of me.
- Don't you dare.

188
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,129
What's with you?

189
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:56,840
Get him!

190
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,009
Catch that thief!

191
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:04,723
Taxi! Stop!

192
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:05,766
Taxi!

193
00:12:09,312 --> 00:12:10,897
Sir, go! Just go!

194
00:12:12,315 --> 00:12:13,774
Where should I take you,

195
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:15,401
sir?

196
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:24,493
<i>Hide, hide</i>

197
00:12:24,494 --> 00:12:25,535
What?

198
00:12:25,536 --> 00:12:27,329
Hey, it's nice to see you!

199
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,123
Take this. Good to see you.

200
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,334
Get that jerk!

201
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:33,252
Got you!

202
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:36,588
It's so nice to see you! How are you here?

203
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:37,548
Who's that?

204
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:43,262
SEOUL SANGWON POLICE STATION

205
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:09,288
I put a lot of effort into making this.

206
00:13:09,872 --> 00:13:10,790
Do you like it?

207
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:14,335
You should've put more effort

208
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:18,047
into building the kindergarten.

209
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:23,928
You've really got nerves of steel.

210
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:25,972
Here's a quiz.

211
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:29,891
There's no evidence anywhere
that you actually embezzled

212
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:30,977
the 17.8 billion won.

213
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,271
So why did I lock you up in here?

214
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,232
This is boring.

215
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,860
Number one, to screw you over.

216
00:13:40,695 --> 00:13:43,698
Number two,
to give you a warning not to act up.

217
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:45,783
Guess the answer.

218
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:49,912
Number three.

219
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:51,956
You're right.

220
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:55,418
You really are smart.

221
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:59,504
Shifting the narrative
and damaging your credibility.

222
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:03,801
People won't be so sure about you

223
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,554
embezzling the 17.8 billion won,

224
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:10,266
but they can immediately accept
you making a fake family.

225
00:14:11,142 --> 00:14:14,811
They'll easily believe
that you were a fraud who faked it

226
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:18,024
to embezzle 17.8 billion won.

227
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:21,819
I'm actually curious.

228
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,654
Did you really think

229
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:28,701
exposing that shoddy construction
would achieve some great justice?

230
00:14:29,619 --> 00:14:32,997
Is there any construction in Korea
that isn't shoddy?

231
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,499
Penthouses in Gangnam worth billions,

232
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,377
nameless apartment complexes
in the middle of nowhere...

233
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:41,631
They're actually all the same.

234
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,384
Is shoddy construction

235
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,678
something to brag about?

236
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:50,263
In the face of shoddy construction,

237
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:52,599
everyone is equal.

238
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,727
There's no rich or poor.

239
00:14:58,481 --> 00:15:00,273
That's how everyone lives.

240
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,233
That's the norm in this business.

241
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:03,110
Commissioner.

242
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:06,905
The grounds for arresting Park
without a warrant

243
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,532
are weak.

244
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:12,370
We did go a little too far.

245
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:21,544
Look at that arrogant piece of shit.

246
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:23,463
He thinks the law and the police

247
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:25,633
are all below him right now.

248
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:30,178
Mr. Lee says he does have a plan,

249
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:33,056
but judging by the way he talks,

250
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:35,434
he's a ticking time bomb.

251
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:37,979
If we get hit by the fallout,

252
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,106
we're done for.

253
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:44,275
Taesan's been under fire lately

254
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:46,654
because of the shoddy
kindergarten construction.

255
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:49,907
Dig into that more properly.

256
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:52,785
We can't keep wiping his ass forever.

257
00:15:53,703 --> 00:15:57,248
I need to have some leverage over him too.

258
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:01,168
Yes, sir.

259
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:06,382
I was going to get you released
for getting the right answer,

260
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,009
but I don't want to.

261
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:11,720
You can take the full 48 hours here

262
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:13,973
to reflect on yourself.

263
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:22,689
I'll tell them to add extra meat
to your soup.

264
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,983
Enjoy your meal.

265
00:16:29,613 --> 00:16:31,240
Your photos look great.

266
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:48,382
Sir, the facility manager
didn't get on the plane.

267
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:53,386
Mr. Kim, stay on your toes.

268
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,765
I'm sorry, sir.
I'll get my men to find him.

269
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:00,853
I wonder where Mr. Choi is hiding.

270
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,897
He'd better not cause trouble

271
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:06,067
if he doesn't want
to end up as fertilizer.

272
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:12,907
<i>When will a sunny day come for me?</i>

273
00:17:13,491 --> 00:17:15,408
<i>- When will...</i>
- Look! Over there!

274
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,787
- Isn't that President Park's father?
- It is.

275
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:21,372
Hey, you fraud!

276
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:24,167
Darn it. I'm so popular,
the ladies won't leave me alone.

277
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,294
- Hello.
- Hello.

278
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,046
Wait, just a moment.

279
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,005
Close it!

280
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:30,381
Hurry!

281
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:31,883
Don't let her in.

282
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,384
Use the next one!

283
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:36,096
Let's all go up together.

284
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:38,099
- How obnoxious.
- There's plenty of space.

285
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:42,310
They stuck them here too?

286
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,230
Everyone already saw these.

287
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,861
YOU THIEVES
DON'T PARK IN OUR PARKING LOT

288
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:54,281
LEAVE, YOU FAKE FAMILY

289
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:04,542
Let's go.

290
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:09,379
EVEN THIEVES NEED A PLACE TO PARK!

291
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,798
THANKS FOR THE MESSAGE

292
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:12,466
Did it hurt?

293
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:18,013
You know, in life,
there are rites of passage.

294
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:23,059
Everyone goes through them at some point.

295
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:25,019
- A trip to the dentist is one of those.
- Mom.

296
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,356
Can we ride a slide before we go home?

297
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:29,483
A slide?

298
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,153
Deal.

299
00:18:35,156 --> 00:18:36,906
- Ha-yul.
- Let's go.

300
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:37,992
Let's go home.

301
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:40,703
- Come on. Let's go.
- Come here.

302
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:43,289
- I want to play some more.
- No.

303
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:46,917
Mom.

304
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,920
Do they hate us

305
00:18:50,588 --> 00:18:53,424
because we're a fake family?

306
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:57,761
Gyeong-buk.

307
00:18:58,721 --> 00:19:00,806
What do you think is fake?

308
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:05,060
Is it real if you're related by blood?

309
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,646
Isn't that what's real?

310
00:19:09,023 --> 00:19:10,273
No.

311
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:14,152
Eating together, worrying together,

312
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:17,113
and staying by each other's side
when things are tough.

313
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:18,490
That's what makes a real family.

314
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,743
The meals we share every day are more real

315
00:19:21,744 --> 00:19:24,412
than the blood ties
those mothers believe in.

316
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:25,289
Got that?

317
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:31,045
There are special families like us.

318
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,133
So

319
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:38,844
keep your chin up, shoulders back,

320
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:42,806
and flash the world a smile!

321
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:47,393
We'll dominate those slides.

322
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:50,606
Let's go!

323
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:05,662
You scared me.

324
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:07,039
Weren't you sleeping?

325
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,758
What is it? You're scaring me.

326
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:20,594
Ha-ri,

327
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,222
let's give them the ledger.

328
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:30,479
Then what about you?

329
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:33,107
I know.

330
00:20:34,275 --> 00:20:35,609
I'll get punished for it.

331
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:40,072
But I'm ready.

332
00:20:44,285 --> 00:20:46,328
Well, I'm not ready.

333
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:48,998
Ha-ri.

334
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:54,043
I started this, so I have to end it.

335
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:56,754
I should take responsibility
for my crimes.

336
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,007
Let's hand over the ledger

337
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,926
and help Mr. Park fight.

338
00:21:02,469 --> 00:21:03,721
Ha-jeong.

339
00:21:06,015 --> 00:21:09,935
Once this is over,
you'd better buckle down and study hard.

340
00:21:10,436 --> 00:21:12,187
I don't know what might happen to me,

341
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:15,357
so you might really have
to take care of me then.

342
00:21:20,446 --> 00:21:21,322
All right.

343
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:24,325
Let's give them the ledger.

344
00:21:38,464 --> 00:21:39,465
Boss!

345
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,013
You've been through so much.

346
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:51,060
How is our family?

347
00:21:52,186 --> 00:21:53,436
Everyone's doing fine.

348
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:55,146
They're all waiting for you.

349
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,774
I was able to hold on thanks to you.

350
00:21:57,775 --> 00:22:01,445
Even after all that fuss,
they released you right away.

351
00:22:02,279 --> 00:22:05,991
That just means
it's going to be worse out here.

352
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,534
Let's go.

353
00:22:11,914 --> 00:22:14,332
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

354
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,377
- Leave True Value!
- Leave True Value!

355
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:19,420
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

356
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:22,090
- Leave True Value!
- Leave True Value!

357
00:22:22,091 --> 00:22:25,259
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

358
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:26,970
- Leave True Value!
- Leave True Value!

359
00:22:27,638 --> 00:22:29,138
The thief is coming!

360
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:33,352
The fraud who made a fake family
to steal from us is coming!

361
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,108
Calm down, everyone!

362
00:22:40,109 --> 00:22:43,903
If you were investigated for embezzlement,
you should be coming out in handcuffs.

363
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:45,446
How did you get released so quickly?

364
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:47,990
Did you hire a powerful lawyer
with the 17.8 billion?

365
00:22:47,991 --> 00:22:49,952
- You thief!
- You thief!

366
00:22:54,998 --> 00:22:57,333
Stop! That's enough!

367
00:22:57,334 --> 00:22:58,835
- Enough?
- Enough?

368
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:01,421
Did you forget what you did to us?

369
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:18,813
I'll bill you 8,000 won

370
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:19,982
for the umbrella later.

371
00:23:20,566 --> 00:23:23,110
Your timing with that umbrella
was a little late.

372
00:23:28,532 --> 00:23:29,740
This is ridiculous.

373
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:32,243
They don't even know how precious salt is.

374
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,828
Do you think the law is a joke?

375
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,830
They let him go
because they found no evidence.

376
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:37,373
What do you think you're doing?

377
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:39,709
Look who's talking.

378
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:41,295
You shameless assholes.

379
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,320
Let me use it too. It's salty.

380
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:08,739
How can you live with yourselves?

381
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:12,992
- You're still pretending to be a couple?
- Seriously.

382
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:15,536
How can you live with yourselves
after making a fake family

383
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:16,495
and stealing from us?

384
00:24:16,496 --> 00:24:19,248
Don't you dare run away with our money!

385
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:21,501
- Don't you dare!
- You thief!

386
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:31,011
I won't run away.

387
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:34,348
I have no intention
of running away with my family.

388
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:36,641
I'm staying right here

389
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:39,352
until we catch the one
who took the 17.8 billion.

390
00:24:39,353 --> 00:24:40,519
What?

391
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,189
Catch who? You're the thief!

392
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:46,902
But if anyone harms my family
in the process,

393
00:24:47,527 --> 00:24:49,529
I'll make them pay in my own way.

394
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,408
You've seen the posters,
so you know what kind of person I am.

395
00:24:54,243 --> 00:24:55,202
Goodness.

396
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:01,792
If you want to find your money,
move aside.

397
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,352
Mr. Choi, drink this.

398
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:25,147
Come on. You need to eat to survive.

399
00:25:25,148 --> 00:25:26,358
No.

400
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:28,944
Just drink it!

401
00:25:29,611 --> 00:25:30,821
Just drink it.

402
00:25:31,822 --> 00:25:33,198
Geez!

403
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:36,492
- What are you doing here?
- Boss!

404
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:38,703
- President Park!
- Boss!

405
00:25:38,704 --> 00:25:40,247
I missed you, Boss.

406
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:43,208
You've gotten so thin.

407
00:25:45,836 --> 00:25:47,295
What's going on here?

408
00:25:47,296 --> 00:25:50,715
I went to talk to Mr. Choi for a moment,

409
00:25:50,716 --> 00:25:52,550
and we ran into each other.

410
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:54,302
But he won't say anything.

411
00:25:54,303 --> 00:25:57,096
President Park! Please help me.

412
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:59,515
They'll be looking everywhere
for me right now.

413
00:25:59,516 --> 00:26:01,767
You jerk. You're the reason our boss...

414
00:26:01,768 --> 00:26:03,352
I'm sorry, President Park.

415
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:05,897
But please help me.

416
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:10,818
I'm not going anywhere
until Mr. Choi tells me

417
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:13,029
where the 17.8 billion went.

418
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:16,240
We have to prove that you're innocent,

419
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:18,993
and that's the only way
we'll get our money back.

420
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:21,413
Don't you agree? Gosh.

421
00:26:22,331 --> 00:26:23,165
Ms. Jang.

422
00:26:25,625 --> 00:26:28,587
Why would you go to such lengths for me?

423
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:31,256
Why? Isn't it obvious?

424
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:36,011
I know better than anyone
that you're innocent.

425
00:26:36,678 --> 00:26:38,263
I'm not innocent.

426
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,390
I...

427
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:43,060
didn't come here to protect
the apartment complex.

428
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:45,687
What are you saying?

429
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:48,023
It's true

430
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:51,360
that I came here to embezzle the fund.

431
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:55,404
Oh my gosh.

432
00:26:55,405 --> 00:26:57,991
Then you mean...

433
00:26:58,575 --> 00:27:00,369
it's true

434
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:02,412
that you embezzled

435
00:27:03,372 --> 00:27:04,581
the 17.8 billion won?

436
00:27:05,165 --> 00:27:06,041
No.

437
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:10,253
When I became the president,
the account was already empty.

438
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:13,965
What are you talking about?

439
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:17,552
You came to embezzle the fund,
but it was already taken?

440
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:19,471
Goodness.

441
00:27:20,597 --> 00:27:23,391
That means Mr. Choi and President Seo

442
00:27:23,392 --> 00:27:26,478
already embezzled it together, doesn't it?

443
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:28,271
Lee Chung-won.

444
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,483
Taesan Construction's president.

445
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:35,069
Who's that? Taesan Construction?

446
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:36,863
The one who built our apartment complex?

447
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:40,992
Are you sure?

448
00:27:41,993 --> 00:27:42,994
Yes.

449
00:27:45,414 --> 00:27:46,914
Those assholes!

450
00:27:46,915 --> 00:27:48,625
They took all our money.

451
00:27:49,459 --> 00:27:50,460
Ms. Jang.

452
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:53,380
I'm sorry.

453
00:27:57,259 --> 00:27:58,592
President Park,

454
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:01,303
I've seen how hard you've worked

455
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:03,722
for our apartment complex.

456
00:28:03,723 --> 00:28:04,766
I believe

457
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:07,226
all of that was sincere.

458
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:09,228
None of that was fake.

459
00:28:09,229 --> 00:28:10,187
Right?

460
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:12,023
So let's use your competence

461
00:28:12,524 --> 00:28:14,693
to find that 17.8 billion won.

462
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:16,278
Find it for us.

463
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:19,405
I won't let you leave True Value

464
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:22,159
until we find that money.

465
00:28:23,326 --> 00:28:24,578
Understand?

466
00:28:36,047 --> 00:28:38,133
Yes, Ms. Jang.

467
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:46,975
They used cheap spray paint.
This is so hard to remove.

468
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:51,270
Gyeong-buk, forget this one.
See the "fraud" at the top?

469
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:54,231
Shoot that instead.

470
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,066
Okay.

471
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,321
Dad!

472
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,364
Dad?

473
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,532
- What are you doing?
- Mr. Park!

474
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:05,910
You're finally back.

475
00:29:05,911 --> 00:29:07,369
You look really thin.

476
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:08,246
PARK HAE-KANG
FRAUD

477
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:11,749
Well...

478
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:14,544
Our door is very popular right now.

479
00:29:15,378 --> 00:29:19,340
Uncle, I'm almost done
erasing the word "thief."

480
00:29:19,341 --> 00:29:20,884
Only the first letter is left.

481
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,933
They did a tacky job, didn't they?

482
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:30,726
Let's go inside. I'm hungry.

483
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:31,895
Right. You must be hungry.

484
00:29:33,396 --> 00:29:35,941
- My fingerprint isn't working.
- It's not locked.

485
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,278
That's so cold.

486
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:43,364
Pull me out! Help me!

487
00:29:43,365 --> 00:29:45,825
Pull me up.

488
00:29:45,826 --> 00:29:47,869
Help...

489
00:29:50,372 --> 00:29:52,040
- Geez!
- You can't just leave me like this!

490
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:54,750
What is all this?

491
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:56,794
- When did you make all this?
- This is for you.

492
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:58,754
How do you know how to make all of this?

493
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:00,673
Everything is so white, though.

494
00:30:00,674 --> 00:30:02,633
This is going to blind my eyes.

495
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:04,552
He put so much effort into this.

496
00:30:04,553 --> 00:30:06,303
He went through a whole sack of beans

497
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:09,014
to make all this tofu
and help his boss get a fresh new start.

498
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:11,600
It's all made with Korean soybeans.
They cost quite a bit.

499
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:13,060
So make sure to eat everything.

500
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:15,521
Right. Soybeans are called
the beef of the fields.

501
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:16,897
Eat up, Mr. Park.

502
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:21,694
You must have taken in a ton of sodium
from all the salt thrown at you.

503
00:30:21,695 --> 00:30:23,280
That's why we didn't season it.

504
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:25,823
Enjoy.

505
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:30,077
With all that red graffiti
and the salt thrown at you,

506
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:32,371
you need this to cleanse your insides.

507
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:34,748
You should regain your strength
and start over.

508
00:30:34,749 --> 00:30:37,960
You know, I wonder
if being in a gang is meant for me.

509
00:30:37,961 --> 00:30:40,462
Whenever I see white tofu,
it reminds me of the old days.

510
00:30:40,463 --> 00:30:41,589
Do you have soy sauce?

511
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:44,675
Just eat whatever is given to you today.

512
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:46,218
All right, Big Guy.

513
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:47,470
Sorry.

514
00:30:48,889 --> 00:30:51,891
Uncle, I'll eat a lot and grow stronger

515
00:30:51,892 --> 00:30:55,186
so I can defeat all the bad guys for you.

516
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:57,856
Okay.

517
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:00,149
When you got taken by the police,

518
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:02,943
I was going to come out
and handle everything,

519
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:05,321
but she stopped me.

520
00:31:05,322 --> 00:31:06,573
You were hiding in the closet.

521
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:08,490
You saw me?

522
00:31:08,491 --> 00:31:09,993
That's why he's the Lizard.

523
00:31:13,413 --> 00:31:14,788
- This is good.
- It's tasty.

524
00:31:14,789 --> 00:31:15,957
It's good.

525
00:31:22,797 --> 00:31:24,799
- Here.
- What are you doing?

526
00:31:34,476 --> 00:31:36,853
TRANSACTION LEDGER

527
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:39,521
You just took the ledger

528
00:31:39,522 --> 00:31:41,191
out of the bookshelf?

529
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:43,860
Yes. I told you I hid it in a safe place.

530
00:31:44,444 --> 00:31:45,736
How is this a safe place?

531
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:48,656
What if Gyeong-nam took out a book
to read for Gyeong-buk and--

532
00:31:48,657 --> 00:31:50,074
You think he'd do that?

533
00:31:50,075 --> 00:31:53,328
These books are so new,
the bindings crack every time I open them.

534
00:31:55,246 --> 00:31:57,457
You're right. This was the safest place.

535
00:32:02,879 --> 00:32:04,505
My sister said she's ready.

536
00:32:04,506 --> 00:32:07,092
She'll take responsibility for her crimes.

537
00:32:11,388 --> 00:32:13,098
I know this wasn't...

538
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:16,309
an easy decision.

539
00:32:17,227 --> 00:32:20,689
I'm putting my sister's life on the line
by giving this to you.

540
00:32:21,481 --> 00:32:24,401
So make sure to crush them

541
00:32:25,318 --> 00:32:27,654
so my sister won't have gone
to prison for nothing.

542
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:57,809
PARKING GARAGE FAN INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

543
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:04,107
PARKING GARAGE LIGHT REPLACEMENT
(REDUCED QUANTITY)

544
00:33:13,116 --> 00:33:15,118
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

545
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:19,122
I'm so happy to be preparing meals
for a criminal who tried to run away.

546
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:21,082
Gosh.

547
00:33:21,666 --> 00:33:23,460
There's too much sauce on this.

548
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:27,464
Open up, Mr. Choi.

549
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,299
Here comes the airplane.

550
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:35,179
I told you I have high cholesterol.

551
00:33:35,180 --> 00:33:38,348
Give me some spinach instead of ham.

552
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:41,935
And I have trouble digesting
anything that isn't organic.

553
00:33:41,936 --> 00:33:44,688
Mr. Choi, this isn't a fancy restaurant.

554
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:47,649
Big Guy, what happens
to picky eaters here?

555
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:49,693
We take them to the rooftop.

556
00:33:49,694 --> 00:33:52,404
- And?
- And they're put in a luggage bag.

557
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:54,574
Fine, I'll eat.

558
00:33:57,494 --> 00:33:59,204
Eat up. Chew thoroughly.

559
00:34:01,164 --> 00:34:02,873
It's a bit salty.

560
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:04,501
I've been on a low-sodium diet.

561
00:34:05,085 --> 00:34:07,586
- Who wants more?
- Me!

562
00:34:07,587 --> 00:34:09,630
Just eat up before I take everything away.

563
00:34:09,631 --> 00:34:12,716
You should be worried about your life,
not your cholesterol.

564
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:14,010
I'm sorry.

565
00:34:16,096 --> 00:34:17,263
- Boss.
- Boss.

566
00:34:17,806 --> 00:34:19,390
- You're here.
- Hello, Boss.

567
00:34:26,356 --> 00:34:27,315
Mr. Choi.

568
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:30,693
The ledger that Ms. Kang Ha-jeong kept

569
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:34,364
only contains
President Seo's name and yours.

570
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:37,741
The notes she wrote
after the embezzled amounts

571
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,868
just say,

572
00:34:39,869 --> 00:34:43,622
"delivered to the facility manager"
or "delivered to President Seo."

573
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:45,792
Lee Chung-won's name
doesn't appear anywhere.

574
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:49,170
Do you know what that means?

575
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:54,175
Who do you think the police will come for
when this is released?

576
00:34:55,009 --> 00:34:58,011
But President Seo is gone from this world.

577
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:01,932
So the sole culprit
who pocketed the entire 17.8 billion

578
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:03,393
will be you, Mr. Choi.

579
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:08,064
No way.

580
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:11,151
Lee Chung-won will make that happen.

581
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:15,446
All he needs is for you to be gone.

582
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,617
Once he gets his hands on this ledger,

583
00:35:20,410 --> 00:35:22,120
he'll be innocent.

584
00:35:27,709 --> 00:35:28,751
What...

585
00:35:29,502 --> 00:35:30,587
Then...

586
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,589
What should I do?

587
00:35:37,719 --> 00:35:40,847
There's been a lot of talk
about Taesan's kindergarten incident.

588
00:35:41,598 --> 00:35:43,265
Get Juan and Hanmin included

589
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:45,435
in the Oman New Town consortium.

590
00:35:46,019 --> 00:35:47,770
Juan and Hanmin?

591
00:35:48,897 --> 00:35:52,025
Aren't they run by old geezers
who only care about background?

592
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:56,279
Why would I include them
in something I set up?

593
00:35:57,155 --> 00:36:00,574
We're not telling you to sit and watch.
We're saying you need insurance.

594
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:02,284
The Oman New Town project

595
00:36:02,285 --> 00:36:05,205
is too big for you to handle on your own.

596
00:36:06,289 --> 00:36:08,208
Don't you trust me?

597
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:11,628
Ever since I worked in demolition,

598
00:36:12,128 --> 00:36:15,839
I've been great
at tearing down other people's lives.

599
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:18,218
But I'm even better at building things.

600
00:36:20,011 --> 00:36:22,639
A single excavator is enough
to take care of this.

601
00:36:23,306 --> 00:36:25,807
I don't get why you keep making a fuss.

602
00:36:25,808 --> 00:36:28,810
You need a background
in the construction industry, Mr. Lee.

603
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:32,398
The smell of the steel pipe
you used to hold still hasn't faded.

604
00:36:34,901 --> 00:36:37,402
I have a pile of documents

605
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:40,948
on how those people
who care so much about background

606
00:36:40,949 --> 00:36:43,533
funneled slush funds
through their sons' development companies.

607
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:46,704
Such documents don't mean anything to us.

608
00:36:47,288 --> 00:36:49,581
Risk management is more important.

609
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:50,541
Mr. Lee.

610
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:54,544
Let me put it more simply
so you can understand.

611
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:56,922
You're nothing but a spare tire to us.

612
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:59,050
A replacement for when things go wrong.

613
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:10,061
You're really hurting my feelings.

614
00:37:10,687 --> 00:37:12,521
Don't take it personally.

615
00:37:12,522 --> 00:37:16,984
We have to worry
about our entire nation, you know.

616
00:37:16,985 --> 00:37:19,111
As long as you work smart,

617
00:37:19,112 --> 00:37:23,324
that spare tire
will keep sitting in our trunk.

618
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:26,368
There's talk about shoddy construction.

619
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:28,788
Shouldn't you handle that issue first?

620
00:37:34,752 --> 00:37:37,005
All right.

621
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:40,258
You can watch how I handle it...

622
00:37:41,551 --> 00:37:42,927
tomorrow.

623
00:37:57,734 --> 00:38:00,569
The patient's condition has worsened.
Contact his guardian.

624
00:38:00,570 --> 00:38:01,612
I'll contact him now.

625
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:03,406
Don't.

626
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:05,116
What?

627
00:38:05,742 --> 00:38:08,494
Don't call Park Hae-kang.

628
00:38:09,579 --> 00:38:10,788
He's busy.

629
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:13,249
But we need your guardian's approval...

630
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:15,043
"Guardian"?

631
00:38:16,502 --> 00:38:20,380
I'm his guardian,
not the other way around.

632
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:22,508
I told you, don't call him...

633
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:37,856
Good evening, Mr. Son.

634
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:39,400
You scared me.

635
00:38:41,361 --> 00:38:44,655
I have something to discuss with you
before you go.

636
00:38:45,156 --> 00:38:46,991
There's nothing to discuss.

637
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:50,411
You didn't bring me a single penny,
let alone ten billion.

638
00:38:51,287 --> 00:38:52,246
This...

639
00:38:52,955 --> 00:38:55,166
is much more valuable than that.

640
00:38:59,045 --> 00:39:01,714
Evidence on Taesan's shoddy construction.

641
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,803
Shoddy construction?

642
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:08,887
Hey.

643
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:12,141
Have you ever seen a construction company
in Korea go under for that?

644
00:39:13,142 --> 00:39:15,018
They'll pay a fine, and that's it.

645
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,938
It's not about going under.

646
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:18,898
It's about becoming useless.

647
00:39:19,524 --> 00:39:21,566
Once Taesan hits the headlines for this

648
00:39:21,567 --> 00:39:22,985
and the president faces the press,

649
00:39:24,112 --> 00:39:25,822
the One Club will collapse.

650
00:39:27,865 --> 00:39:28,907
What?

651
00:39:28,908 --> 00:39:31,411
Your ticket to join the club is gone.

652
00:39:32,245 --> 00:39:34,872
How long will you keep rowing
on a sinking ship?

653
00:39:35,915 --> 00:39:37,791
Use this evidence to climb a new ladder

654
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:41,253
as a detective who took down
a conglomerate president.

655
00:39:41,254 --> 00:39:44,256
What better gift could there be
for the commissioner?

656
00:39:44,257 --> 00:39:48,219
You're holding leverage
that could rattle Lee Chung-won.

657
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:58,855
Can you really rattle Lee Chung-won?

658
00:39:59,939 --> 00:40:01,607
I'm going to bring him down.

659
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:05,570
So stop holding my old boss hostage

660
00:40:06,112 --> 00:40:07,864
and release him on medical bail.

661
00:40:18,166 --> 00:40:20,209
I'll decide once I see the results.

662
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:51,324
Why are you looking at me so sadly?

663
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:53,993
You're making me uncomfortable.

664
00:40:55,411 --> 00:40:56,370
I wasn't.

665
00:40:58,581 --> 00:41:00,750
I was glaring at you viciously.

666
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:04,295
Don't look so glum.

667
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:07,381
You're not the one dying.

668
00:41:08,716 --> 00:41:09,800
I'm not looking glum.

669
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:12,553
I look really handsome right now.

670
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:17,183
Take good care of yourself.

671
00:41:18,267 --> 00:41:20,770
You're still young.
You should stay in shape.

672
00:41:25,066 --> 00:41:26,526
Is something wrong?

673
00:41:30,238 --> 00:41:31,531
No, of course not.

674
00:41:32,406 --> 00:41:34,659
I'm just sorry
I couldn't get you released quickly.

675
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:38,746
You're not going to tell me

676
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:41,666
what you're up to?

677
00:41:43,334 --> 00:41:44,210
I...

678
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:48,881
chose someone else instead of you.

679
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:51,259
<i>Mr. Park.</i>

680
00:41:52,134 --> 00:41:53,426
Please...

681
00:41:53,427 --> 00:41:55,513
Please help my sister.

682
00:41:57,848 --> 00:42:00,851
Is she young and pretty?

683
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:05,898
It's not like that.

684
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:11,028
Well, I'm old and not pretty.

685
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:15,323
It's natural for me
to be pushed down the priority list.

686
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:16,867
You did the right thing.

687
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:21,372
You'll be released soon.

688
00:42:23,291 --> 00:42:24,875
I'm working on it,

689
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:27,837
so hold on just a little while longer.

690
00:42:35,011 --> 00:42:36,429
You know,

691
00:42:37,805 --> 00:42:41,559
you're a man who instinctively judges
what's right or wrong.

692
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:45,605
You pretend to be a bad guy,

693
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:48,983
but you've got a better heart than anyone.

694
00:42:50,359 --> 00:42:51,277
No.

695
00:42:52,737 --> 00:42:54,446
I do a lot of bad things.

696
00:42:54,447 --> 00:42:55,615
I am a bad guy.

697
00:42:57,074 --> 00:43:01,996
You're the type to save people
even if you planned to do something bad.

698
00:43:03,205 --> 00:43:04,790
I know you.

699
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:06,959
So...

700
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:11,714
do whatever you want.

701
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:15,800
There's no need to hesitate because of me.

702
00:43:15,801 --> 00:43:19,305
And don't make bad choices
because of me either.

703
00:43:19,889 --> 00:43:23,100
If I become an obstacle
to what you're trying to do,

704
00:43:23,809 --> 00:43:28,064
I won't be able to rest in peace.

705
00:43:28,939 --> 00:43:29,856
Geez.

706
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:31,776
Why do you keep talking about dying?

707
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:34,402
You should enjoy life by my side first.

708
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:36,614
So quit the nonsense and stay strong.

709
00:43:37,573 --> 00:43:40,910
I won't let you go like this.

710
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:43,704
You punk.

711
00:43:45,748 --> 00:43:49,502
You've been through a lot
being my son all these years.

712
00:43:53,172 --> 00:43:54,590
Thank you.

713
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:01,806
You're making me cringe. I'm leaving.

714
00:44:02,848 --> 00:44:04,433
Make sure to eat well.

715
00:44:06,477 --> 00:44:08,396
I love you, son.

716
00:44:40,761 --> 00:44:44,890
WE SINCERELY APOLOGIZE
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION

717
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:53,523
What are they up to,
calling all these reporters here?

718
00:44:53,524 --> 00:44:55,442
- What's going on?
- You didn't hear anything?

719
00:44:55,443 --> 00:44:57,068
They never said anything.

720
00:44:57,069 --> 00:44:58,194
Let's see what they say.

721
00:44:58,195 --> 00:44:59,488
Sure, let's see.

722
00:45:12,543 --> 00:45:15,753
Isn't he the guy who rode
the elevator with us last time?

723
00:45:15,754 --> 00:45:17,297
Yes, the penthouse.

724
00:45:17,298 --> 00:45:19,507
- He's the president of Taesan.
- No way.

725
00:45:19,508 --> 00:45:21,050
You didn't know, right?

726
00:45:21,051 --> 00:45:23,970
Is there a specific reason
why you're apologizing here

727
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:25,680
instead of at the company headquarters?

728
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:28,141
Some are saying
this is just a show for the cameras.

729
00:45:28,142 --> 00:45:29,351
Give us a comment.

730
00:45:38,402 --> 00:45:39,653
I am standing here today...

731
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:43,240
not as Taesan's president,

732
00:45:44,492 --> 00:45:47,912
but as a resident of True Value State.

733
00:45:48,954 --> 00:45:50,246
I believe it is my duty

734
00:45:50,247 --> 00:45:53,542
to apologize at the location
where my neighbors and their children

735
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:55,835
could have been harmed.

736
00:45:55,836 --> 00:45:57,003
An apology isn't enough!

737
00:45:57,004 --> 00:45:59,214
Our kids almost died, you fraud!

738
00:45:59,215 --> 00:46:02,217
How can you build
a kindergarten like that?

739
00:46:02,218 --> 00:46:04,053
Don't you even have a family?

740
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:08,182
The investigation

741
00:46:08,682 --> 00:46:11,434
found that our subcontractor
used improper construction methods

742
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:13,353
and failed to oversee the work properly.

743
00:46:13,354 --> 00:46:16,773
Are you blaming everything
on your subcontractor?

744
00:46:16,774 --> 00:46:19,943
It's Taesan's fault for not managing
the construction properly.

745
00:46:19,944 --> 00:46:22,154
Don't you dare make excuses!

746
00:46:24,573 --> 00:46:26,242
How shameless!

747
00:46:27,493 --> 00:46:28,702
You're absolutely right.

748
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:30,871
It was my oversight.

749
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:36,085
That is why Taesan
has made a major decision.

750
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:38,878
We will demolish
the kindergarten immediately

751
00:46:38,879 --> 00:46:41,464
and rebuild it
into one of the finest kindergartens

752
00:46:41,465 --> 00:46:43,551
with Korea's top architects.

753
00:46:44,969 --> 00:46:47,930
- That will take ages.
- That'll take forever.

754
00:46:48,597 --> 00:46:50,557
And during the construction period,

755
00:46:50,558 --> 00:46:54,186
I'll send our children
to a top-tier English kindergarten nearby.

756
00:46:54,937 --> 00:46:58,273
And of course,
Taesan will pay for the tuition

757
00:46:58,274 --> 00:47:00,442
and the shuttle bus fees.

758
00:47:00,943 --> 00:47:02,777
Their tuition
is over three million a month.

759
00:47:02,778 --> 00:47:05,738
- Three million? That's insane.
- It's very expensive.

760
00:47:05,739 --> 00:47:08,367
Taesan promises to take care

761
00:47:09,868 --> 00:47:11,786
of our children's safety and education.

762
00:47:11,787 --> 00:47:13,413
Once again, we apologize.

763
00:47:13,414 --> 00:47:14,582
We ask for your trust.

764
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:21,504
At least they're taking responsibility.

765
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:25,133
Right. Sending them
to an English kindergarten changes things.

766
00:47:25,134 --> 00:47:26,593
- What now?
- We should trust them.

767
00:47:26,594 --> 00:47:29,263
- Do we give them another chance?
- This doesn't feel right.

768
00:47:31,223 --> 00:47:32,683
Trust them? Are you kidding me?

769
00:47:55,581 --> 00:47:57,081
President Park...

770
00:47:57,082 --> 00:47:59,542
What's he doing? Why is he holding that?

771
00:47:59,543 --> 00:48:00,419
Do we call the cops?

772
00:48:02,046 --> 00:48:03,297
What is that?

773
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,549
President Lee Chung-won.

774
00:48:06,342 --> 00:48:08,093
Do you think
building another kindergarten...

775
00:48:11,138 --> 00:48:12,640
will solve everything?

776
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:15,476
- Open the door!
- Open this!

777
00:48:16,101 --> 00:48:18,019
Je-gil, can't you hurry up?

778
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:20,396
- They'll break down the door at this rate!
- Almost done.

779
00:48:20,397 --> 00:48:21,732
He always says that.

780
00:48:22,274 --> 00:48:24,443
He's right in front of Lee Chung-won now.

781
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:28,655
LIVE BROADCAST IN PROGRESS

782
00:48:28,656 --> 00:48:32,575
Yes! Every wall pad, elevator display,
and even the emergency speakers

783
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:33,661
are connected now.

784
00:48:34,244 --> 00:48:35,161
Boss.

785
00:48:35,162 --> 00:48:37,247
Everyone in this apartment complex
is watching now!

786
00:48:38,832 --> 00:48:39,708
All right. Be careful.

787
00:48:41,794 --> 00:48:43,087
Watch out.

788
00:48:49,551 --> 00:48:50,844
Move!

789
00:48:55,974 --> 00:48:57,017
One.

790
00:49:00,437 --> 00:49:01,480
Two.

791
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:05,192
How many times
do I need to hit it to tear it down?

792
00:49:06,777 --> 00:49:08,278
Wait, President Park!

793
00:49:19,248 --> 00:49:21,165
What's that doing there?

794
00:49:21,166 --> 00:49:22,792
It's filled with trash.

795
00:49:22,793 --> 00:49:23,877
What is that doing there?

796
00:49:25,045 --> 00:49:26,296
Where's the rebar?

797
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:30,925
That must be from a garbage dump!

798
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:33,804
Did they fill the walls with trash?

799
00:49:35,681 --> 00:49:39,350
<i>Is there any construction in Korea
that isn't shoddy?</i>

800
00:49:39,351 --> 00:49:41,729
They're actually all the same.

801
00:49:42,312 --> 00:49:43,647
Is shoddy construction

802
00:49:44,481 --> 00:49:45,607
something to brag about?

803
00:49:47,401 --> 00:49:49,527
This is the basement
mechanical room floor plan.

804
00:49:49,528 --> 00:49:52,113
The pipes go through here.

805
00:49:52,114 --> 00:49:53,448
It's right below this.

806
00:49:53,449 --> 00:49:54,782
- This place here.
- Right.

807
00:49:54,783 --> 00:49:57,535
This is likely
to have construction defects.

808
00:49:57,536 --> 00:49:59,871
Every part you can't see
was probably built poorly.

809
00:49:59,872 --> 00:50:01,539
<i>Even if they leave out some rebar rods,</i>

810
00:50:01,540 --> 00:50:04,208
<i>people can't tell
if they're covered up nicely.</i>

811
00:50:04,209 --> 00:50:07,211
It should be detecting the rebar,
but it's quiet.

812
00:50:07,212 --> 00:50:08,546
Shouldn't there be rebar here?

813
00:50:08,547 --> 00:50:09,756
Look.

814
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:11,591
It's just crumbling like this.

815
00:50:11,592 --> 00:50:13,552
They only put rebar where it's visible.

816
00:50:14,052 --> 00:50:15,678
<i>Where does this wall lead to?</i>

817
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:17,221
<i>This connects all the way</i>

818
00:50:17,222 --> 00:50:20,434
<i>to the conference room's main wall.</i>

819
00:50:24,271 --> 00:50:25,189
All right.

820
00:50:29,568 --> 00:50:30,944
Let me ask you one question.

821
00:50:31,528 --> 00:50:34,489
Are you going to demolish
all 9,800 apartments here

822
00:50:34,490 --> 00:50:35,657
and rebuild them again?

823
00:50:46,001 --> 00:50:47,377
President Lee Chung-won.

824
00:50:53,342 --> 00:50:57,804
Why do you think
you're being humiliated here?

825
00:50:57,805 --> 00:50:58,847
It's a quiz.

826
00:51:00,808 --> 00:51:01,683
Park Hae-kang.

827
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:05,646
Do you even know what you've done?

828
00:51:06,438 --> 00:51:09,441
Number one, because Park Hae-kang
is crazier than expected.

829
00:51:10,108 --> 00:51:12,819
Number two, because you're
more careless than expected.

830
00:51:12,820 --> 00:51:14,029
Guess the answer.

831
00:51:15,197 --> 00:51:17,031
What's number three?

832
00:51:17,032 --> 00:51:18,408
Number three,

833
00:51:19,159 --> 00:51:22,037
because you got trapped
in your own narrative.

834
00:51:23,413 --> 00:51:25,207
And it's time for you to go down.

835
00:51:29,294 --> 00:51:31,420
Listen carefully.

836
00:51:31,421 --> 00:51:33,507
Now, when people hear
the name Lee Chung-won,

837
00:51:34,132 --> 00:51:36,050
they'll only think of shoddy construction,

838
00:51:36,051 --> 00:51:37,635
trash walls, and lies.

839
00:51:37,636 --> 00:51:40,138
They won't think of you any other way.

840
00:51:40,889 --> 00:51:44,184
Nobody will trust a word you say now.

841
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:54,611
I'll treat you to soup later,

842
00:51:55,112 --> 00:51:56,989
with extra meat.

843
00:51:58,490 --> 00:51:59,615
President Lee!

844
00:51:59,616 --> 00:52:01,118
Will you take responsibility?

845
00:52:22,514 --> 00:52:25,517
How dare a lowlife thug do this to me?

846
00:52:29,730 --> 00:52:31,565
GONGYEONG DAILY LEE SANG-GYU

847
00:52:33,984 --> 00:52:35,694
Great timing.

848
00:52:37,404 --> 00:52:39,990
That video aired from the conference room...

849
00:52:40,616 --> 00:52:42,909
Make sure not a single article
is released about it.

850
00:52:42,910 --> 00:52:44,703
I'll give you as much as you want.

851
00:52:45,329 --> 00:52:47,705
The reporters at the scene
have already published articles.

852
00:52:47,706 --> 00:52:48,998
It's too late.

853
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:51,417
"Taesan trash wall"
is the top trending search

854
00:52:51,418 --> 00:52:52,585
on every portal right now.

855
00:52:52,586 --> 00:52:54,337
Then get those articles taken down!

856
00:52:54,338 --> 00:52:56,505
Call the presidents of every portal.

857
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:59,008
No, call the elders

858
00:52:59,009 --> 00:53:01,135
and stop all the articles!

859
00:53:01,136 --> 00:53:04,013
<i>Everyone's releasing articles about it.
We can't afford to miss this.</i>

860
00:53:04,014 --> 00:53:05,599
<i>You crossed the line this time.</i>

861
00:53:12,481 --> 00:53:14,274
Park Hae-kang, that bastard...

862
00:53:15,609 --> 00:53:17,819
He's really blowing everything up.

863
00:53:19,988 --> 00:53:21,447
TAESAN'S SHODDY CONSTRUCTION EXPOSED

864
00:53:21,448 --> 00:53:23,074
You all saw the video, right?

865
00:53:23,075 --> 00:53:26,786
Mr. Park came in
dragging that sledgehammer,

866
00:53:26,787 --> 00:53:28,663
dug his toes in,

867
00:53:28,664 --> 00:53:30,915
drew all his strength up from his core,

868
00:53:30,916 --> 00:53:33,668
then swung that sledgehammer like this

869
00:53:33,669 --> 00:53:37,254
and jumped, slamming it against the wall,

870
00:53:37,255 --> 00:53:40,383
and it came crumbling down
with a cloud of dust...

871
00:53:40,384 --> 00:53:43,135
And instead of the rebar,

872
00:53:43,136 --> 00:53:44,888
a load of trash

873
00:53:46,014 --> 00:53:47,224
came spilling out.

874
00:53:47,933 --> 00:53:50,852
That was the most amazing video
I've seen this year.

875
00:53:52,396 --> 00:53:56,066
He really is my son. That was so cool.

876
00:53:56,942 --> 00:53:59,485
Korea really is an internet powerhouse.

877
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:00,945
The video's already going viral.

878
00:54:00,946 --> 00:54:03,197
Really? Wow!

879
00:54:03,198 --> 00:54:05,909
Would Taesan be able to survive this?

880
00:54:09,579 --> 00:54:11,747
- They're done for.
- They're done for.

881
00:54:11,748 --> 00:54:13,624
It's checkmate.

882
00:54:13,625 --> 00:54:15,544
Game, set, and match.

883
00:54:16,503 --> 00:54:17,837
There's no way out.

884
00:54:17,838 --> 00:54:20,006
Justice has been served.

885
00:54:20,007 --> 00:54:23,676
<i>The hashtag "Taesan survivor"
is trending on social media</i>

886
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:27,471
<i>as a protest against Taesan's
shoddy apartment construction.</i>

887
00:54:27,472 --> 00:54:31,058
<i>There are growing demands
for safety checks on all apartments...</i>

888
00:54:31,059 --> 00:54:32,102
"Survivor"?

889
00:54:33,186 --> 00:54:36,230
They've been eating
and sleeping comfortably

890
00:54:36,231 --> 00:54:37,566
in the apartments I built,

891
00:54:38,734 --> 00:54:41,527
and now they're pretending to be victims?

892
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:42,738
Sir,

893
00:54:43,447 --> 00:54:46,782
Taesan lost a trillion won in market value
just ten minutes into trading.

894
00:54:46,783 --> 00:54:48,910
Our treasury stock
won't be enough to stop the slide.

895
00:54:50,954 --> 00:54:54,206
This is all because you couldn't
even get rid of one lousy thug!

896
00:54:54,207 --> 00:54:55,332
I'm sorry, sir.

897
00:54:55,333 --> 00:54:58,795
Neither the media nor the prosecution
is willing to make a move right now.

898
00:55:06,053 --> 00:55:07,137
I see.

899
00:55:07,888 --> 00:55:09,431
All of them

900
00:55:10,390 --> 00:55:12,851
are hiding like cowards.

901
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:14,728
Sir?

902
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:19,066
If money won't solve this,
I'll change my methods.

903
00:55:19,983 --> 00:55:22,444
If a thug set this up...

904
00:55:24,196 --> 00:55:27,574
I should play by his rules
so I won't feel bad about it.

905
00:55:30,285 --> 00:55:31,661
Don't you agree, Mr. Kim?

906
00:55:39,294 --> 00:55:41,129
MR. SON, SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

907
00:55:44,674 --> 00:55:46,300
Did you see the news?

908
00:55:46,301 --> 00:55:48,719
You created quite the mess.

909
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:50,472
I've just been summoned
by the commissioner.

910
00:55:51,389 --> 00:55:53,641
It's your turn to secure
the investigation into Taesan

911
00:55:53,642 --> 00:55:55,644
and become a hero.

912
00:55:56,144 --> 00:55:59,647
I'll make sure Lee Chung-won
ends up in front of the cameras,

913
00:55:59,648 --> 00:56:00,982
so you'd better watch your mouth.

914
00:56:01,566 --> 00:56:04,777
As long as my old boss is released,
I'll keep my mouth shut.

915
00:56:04,778 --> 00:56:06,904
<i>All right.
I just submitted the paperwork for it.</i>

916
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:08,073
Get it done quickly.

917
00:56:16,081 --> 00:56:17,082
I'll answer it.

918
00:56:21,253 --> 00:56:23,380
Can you step out for a moment?

919
00:56:24,297 --> 00:56:26,591
Come on out. It's okay.

920
00:56:34,516 --> 00:56:36,100
What are you waiting for?

921
00:56:36,101 --> 00:56:38,978
You should say the lines you prepared.

922
00:56:38,979 --> 00:56:40,563
President Park,

923
00:56:40,564 --> 00:56:43,108
I'm sorry.

924
00:56:43,817 --> 00:56:45,151
We're sorry.

925
00:56:45,152 --> 00:56:48,279
- I apologize for throwing salt at you.
- I'm sorry.

926
00:56:48,280 --> 00:56:49,864
- We're sorry.
- We're sorry.

927
00:56:49,865 --> 00:56:51,907
- We were too much.
- We're sorry.

928
00:56:51,908 --> 00:56:53,326
- We apologize.
- We're sorry.

929
00:56:56,371 --> 00:56:58,164
Well, if you've apologized,

930
00:56:58,165 --> 00:57:00,291
you should get to the main point.

931
00:57:00,292 --> 00:57:01,709
President Park,

932
00:57:01,710 --> 00:57:04,420
everyone in our building has agreed

933
00:57:04,421 --> 00:57:06,714
to tear down all the walls
starting tomorrow.

934
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:08,717
Our building agreed to do it too.

935
00:57:09,885 --> 00:57:11,219
And if you find trash inside?

936
00:57:12,846 --> 00:57:14,889
What if your property value drops?

937
00:57:14,890 --> 00:57:16,724
A safe home for our kids

938
00:57:16,725 --> 00:57:19,060
is more important than our property value.

939
00:57:19,561 --> 00:57:23,731
And you're the only one
who can bring Taesan down.

940
00:57:23,732 --> 00:57:25,900
So please take the lead.

941
00:57:25,901 --> 00:57:28,068
We'll support you.

942
00:57:28,069 --> 00:57:30,279
- Please, President Park.
- Please help us.

943
00:57:30,280 --> 00:57:31,447
Please help us.

944
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:32,949
Please help us out.

945
00:57:33,533 --> 00:57:34,533
What was that?

946
00:57:34,534 --> 00:57:37,036
Please help us.

947
00:57:37,037 --> 00:57:39,206
- Help us.
- Give us a chance.

948
00:57:41,333 --> 00:57:45,961
We've decided to fight together
until the end,

949
00:57:45,962 --> 00:57:46,963
so, President Park,

950
00:57:47,797 --> 00:57:49,799
let's do this together.

951
00:57:51,218 --> 00:57:52,134
All right.

952
00:57:52,135 --> 00:57:54,470
But I'm doing this my way.

953
00:57:54,471 --> 00:57:57,139
I want you all to have my back,

954
00:57:57,140 --> 00:58:00,977
so no one can touch my sledgehammer.

955
00:58:01,645 --> 00:58:03,479
Let's protect True Value.

956
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:04,606
Yes!

957
00:58:05,190 --> 00:58:07,734
- Let's protect True Value, everyone!
- Let's do it!

958
00:58:15,242 --> 00:58:16,076
Mr. Kim.

959
00:58:16,910 --> 00:58:18,036
Yes, sir.

960
00:58:18,995 --> 00:58:21,998
Do you know when you feel
the most despair in your life?

961
00:58:22,916 --> 00:58:27,045
When the ground collapses beneath you
just as you think you've made it.

962
00:58:29,214 --> 00:58:31,216
Park Hae-kang
is in that situation right now.

963
00:58:32,217 --> 00:58:34,636
He's all excited, thinking he's won.

964
00:58:41,685 --> 00:58:42,978
This smells nice.

965
00:58:44,729 --> 00:58:47,524
Just wait. I'll be there soon.

966
00:58:57,075 --> 00:58:58,451
Is that you, Hae-kang?

967
00:58:59,995 --> 00:59:01,580
Why are you here again?

968
00:59:08,795 --> 00:59:11,505
Mr. Park is a bit busy,

969
00:59:11,506 --> 00:59:13,341
so I came instead.

970
00:59:18,096 --> 00:59:20,223
Who are you?

971
00:59:20,974 --> 00:59:24,226
Mr. Park said he cares about you a lot,

972
00:59:24,227 --> 00:59:26,146
so I was curious.

973
00:59:32,569 --> 00:59:36,448
Mr. Park is going through a lot
because of you.

974
00:59:37,115 --> 00:59:39,366
You don't share a drop of blood,

975
00:59:39,367 --> 00:59:41,328
yet he's ruining his own life

976
00:59:42,287 --> 00:59:45,081
over so-called loyalty.

977
00:59:47,125 --> 00:59:48,460
He's always been

978
00:59:50,003 --> 00:59:52,547
foolishly loyal.

979
00:59:57,594 --> 00:59:58,762
Who...

980
00:59:59,679 --> 01:00:00,597
are you?

981
01:00:01,931 --> 01:00:05,393
I'm here to clean up the garbage
that he hasn't been able to get rid of.

982
01:00:06,561 --> 01:00:08,188
Garbage?

983
01:00:11,191 --> 01:00:12,483
It's foolish,

984
01:00:12,484 --> 01:00:15,487
clinging to a losing card until the end.

985
01:00:16,029 --> 01:00:17,530
My mom did that too.

986
01:00:18,156 --> 01:00:21,326
She stood her ground
against the demolition crew swinging bats

987
01:00:21,910 --> 01:00:24,996
just to protect a house
that was already falling apart.

988
01:00:25,789 --> 01:00:28,166
She got carried out, covered in blood,

989
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:31,419
but the world was so quiet.

990
01:00:32,504 --> 01:00:33,755
That's when I realized

991
01:00:35,340 --> 01:00:37,508
that I shouldn't take away the bats.

992
01:00:37,509 --> 01:00:39,719
I should keep the ones wielding them

993
01:00:40,220 --> 01:00:42,847
beneath my feet.

994
01:00:44,724 --> 01:00:45,934
You're...

995
01:00:47,560 --> 01:00:49,062
really...

996
01:00:50,522 --> 01:00:51,439
pitiful.

997
01:01:00,490 --> 01:01:02,075
What did you just say?

998
01:01:05,078 --> 01:01:08,206
You've piled up mountains of money,

999
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:11,459
but your heart

1000
01:01:12,711 --> 01:01:16,923
is still that of the little boy
at the demolition site,

1001
01:01:18,049 --> 01:01:20,927
trembling in fear.

1002
01:01:23,555 --> 01:01:25,724
You're still a pitiful boy

1003
01:01:26,641 --> 01:01:29,894
scattering poison everywhere

1004
01:01:31,187 --> 01:01:33,773
so you won't...

1005
01:01:37,068 --> 01:01:38,236
get beaten.

1006
01:01:40,530 --> 01:01:44,242
Those are pretty harsh words
coming from a dying man.

1007
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:47,662
"Pitiful"?

1008
01:02:02,385 --> 01:02:05,722
That pitiful boy will give you a present.

1009
01:02:16,399 --> 01:02:18,485
PARK ****-MAN

1010
01:02:24,574 --> 01:02:28,828
<i>You're really pitiful.</i>

1011
01:02:29,329 --> 01:02:32,665
<i>You're still a pitiful boy
scattering poison everywhere</i>

1012
01:02:33,583 --> 01:02:36,127
<i>so you won't...</i>

1013
01:02:37,170 --> 01:02:38,213
<i>get beaten.</i>

1014
01:03:53,288 --> 01:03:54,622
Yong-man.

1015
01:03:55,832 --> 01:03:56,791
Yong-man.

1016
01:03:57,667 --> 01:03:59,002
I'm here.

1017
01:04:01,462 --> 01:04:02,338
Yong-man.

1018
01:04:03,590 --> 01:04:05,173
Yong-man, it's me.

1019
01:04:05,174 --> 01:04:06,092
Yong-man!

1020
01:04:16,477 --> 01:04:17,395
Someone...

1021
01:04:18,021 --> 01:04:18,980
Excuse me.

1022
01:04:20,982 --> 01:04:22,191
Anyone?

1023
01:04:28,907 --> 01:04:30,491
Please save Yong-man.

1024
01:04:31,618 --> 01:04:33,286
Please save him...

1025
01:04:36,247 --> 01:04:39,042
Please save Yong-man...

1026
01:04:42,503 --> 01:04:45,590
Someone, please save him...

1027
01:05:30,802 --> 01:05:32,303
CONDOLENCE BOX

1028
01:05:33,805 --> 01:05:34,806
What?

1029
01:05:37,308 --> 01:05:38,768
LEE CHUNG-WON

1030
01:06:30,778 --> 01:06:33,114
I was startled

1031
01:06:33,990 --> 01:06:35,575
when I heard the news.

1032
01:06:36,367 --> 01:06:37,702
I heard

1033
01:06:38,411 --> 01:06:41,164
he was like a father to you.

1034
01:06:42,582 --> 01:06:44,375
You must be devastated.

1035
01:06:49,088 --> 01:06:50,715
I happened to be there

1036
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:53,968
in his final moments.

1037
01:06:56,345 --> 01:06:58,056
Why did you do it?

1038
01:06:59,057 --> 01:07:01,683
You should have been there for him

1039
01:07:01,684 --> 01:07:03,936
when he passed away.

1040
01:07:05,480 --> 01:07:07,190
But don't worry.

1041
01:07:08,608 --> 01:07:10,943
He didn't suffer when he passed.

1042
01:07:12,528 --> 01:07:13,362
You...

1043
01:07:17,366 --> 01:07:18,659
What did you do?

1044
01:07:22,538 --> 01:07:23,372
Huh?

1045
01:07:28,711 --> 01:07:30,254
Remember how I said

1046
01:07:30,838 --> 01:07:33,174
hangnails should be ripped off,
even if you bleed?

1047
01:07:34,550 --> 01:07:37,094
He seemed to be a hangnail

1048
01:07:37,095 --> 01:07:39,806
in your life.

1049
01:07:40,765 --> 01:07:44,060
So I ripped it off for you.

1050
01:07:45,311 --> 01:07:46,896
Don't you feel relieved now?

1051
01:07:52,693 --> 01:07:54,862
I offer my deepest...

1052
01:07:56,197 --> 01:07:57,698
condolences.

1053
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:35,027
THE APARTMENT JOB

1054
01:08:59,135 --> 01:09:00,135
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

1055
01:09:00,136 --> 01:09:02,345
<i>You have to win, no matter what it takes.</i>

1056
01:09:02,346 --> 01:09:03,597
<i>That's what you have to do.</i>

1057
01:09:03,598 --> 01:09:06,600
I'll live my life
proving that you were right.

1058
01:09:06,601 --> 01:09:09,895
<i>Cut the prices
of the Oman New Town units in half.</i>

1059
01:09:09,896 --> 01:09:11,354
We will be reborn.

1060
01:09:11,355 --> 01:09:15,233
Shouldn't we scrape together
every last penny to save our company?

1061
01:09:15,234 --> 01:09:17,277
Please have mercy, sir!

1062
01:09:17,278 --> 01:09:19,696
<i>Taegowon isn't just a tree farm, is it?</i>

1063
01:09:19,697 --> 01:09:22,616
<i>Whenever we took money out of the fund,
we delivered it to Taegowon.</i>

1064
01:09:22,617 --> 01:09:24,826
<i>Then our 17.8 billion should be there too.</i>

1065
01:09:24,827 --> 01:09:26,036
<i>Should we steal it back?</i>

1066
01:09:26,037 --> 01:09:27,704
<i>Yes. He values that more than his life.</i>

1067
01:09:27,705 --> 01:09:30,332
<i>They have such pretty nameplates
for every tree.</i>

1068
01:09:30,333 --> 01:09:32,459
Do you have a death wish?

1069
01:09:32,460 --> 01:09:33,919
Should I try digging?

1070
01:09:33,920 --> 01:09:35,712
<i>Change all the license plates.</i>

1071
01:09:35,713 --> 01:09:38,048
<i>Move everything,
and don't leave a speck of dirt behind.</i>

1072
01:09:38,049 --> 01:09:41,259
<i>But Taesan's warehouse will be too risky.</i>

1073
01:09:41,260 --> 01:09:42,510
That one!

1074
01:09:42,511 --> 01:09:45,055
<i>I know a place.
Somewhere no one can even imagine.</i>

1075
01:09:45,056 --> 01:09:46,724
<i>Are you ready? Run!</i>

1076
01:09:48,726 --> 01:09:50,728
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
